  "details": "https://feedback.vrchat.com/avatar-dynamics-reports-and-feedback/p/feedback-allow-physbone-world-immobile-setting-to-reduce-rotational-movement\nThis can be merged into this request. I've been told that the behavior I'm looking for is the ability to change the root transform used within the World Immobility setting, so that instead of the PhysBone having motion with offsets from the avatar root, the motion is relative to another transform. The ultimate goal is a PhysBone hierarchy that doesn't have motion while the avatar is moving or turning, but does have motion when it's parent gains offsets.\nThis will allow props in the armature that use PhysBones to not have undesirable movement while turning. Please!",
